Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 17:35:14 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: reconnect the last phone until it's in range

"Autoconnect Last Device" (Settings > Android Auto) made one attempt
when Dash started. The phone was often not reachable yet (its Bluetooth
still starting, or not in the car yet), and nothing tried again.

- The last phone is the last paired phone that connected, by any route
  (before, only a finished wireless Android Auto handshake saved it).
- Once the adapter is up, Dash connects it (all profiles, so calls,
  music and wireless Android Auto follow), every 10 s for two minutes,
  then every minute, until a phone is connected. Asynchronous: the UI
  never waits on it.
- The adapter can become usable after Dash starts (a UART controller
  loading its firmware): Bluetooth now follows usableAdapterChanged, so
  the Bluetooth player and this work then too.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [Ozark OS behaviour]
